----- COBOL program to count records in a file ------
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. COUNTREC.

ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
   SELECT INPUT-FILE ASSING TO INFILE 
   ORGANIZATION IS SEQUENTIAL 
   FILE STATUS IS WS-FS.

DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD INPUT-FILE.
01 INUT-REC PIC X(80).

WORKING-STOARGE SECTION.
01 WS-COUNT PIC 9(5) VALUE ZERO.
01 WS-FS PIC XX.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
OPEN INPUT INPUT-FILE 

PERFORM UNTIL WS-EOF = 'Y'
   READ EMPFILE 
     AT END 
         MOVE 'Y' TO WS-EOF 
     NOT AT END 
        ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT 
   END-READ
END-PERFORM 

DISPLAY WS-COUNT.

*****************************************************************************8
Simple explanation for interviewer
1. OPEN INPUT – Opens the input file.
2. READ – Reads one record at a time.
3. ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT – Increments the counter for every record.
4. AT END – Stops reading when the end of file is reached.
5. CLOSE – Closes the file.
6. DISPLAY – Displays the total record count.
Important interview point: File status 10 indicates End Of File (EOF).

Remember this logic:

READ INPUT-FILE
    AT END
        SET EOF TO TRUE
    NOT AT END
        ADD 1 TO WS-COUNT
END-READ

